The problem is about coloring a grid graph where edges connect not just adjacent vertices but also diagonals of unit squares. This means for any two vertices $(i,j)$ and $(k,l)$, they are connected by an edge if they are adjacent horizontally/vertically OR if they are diagonal neighbors.

Looking at the image description mentioned - it says the edges are "all the sides and diagonals of the grid's unit squares". This means each vertex is connected to:
- Up, down, left, right neighbors (sides)
- All diagonal neighbors (diagonals)

So for a vertex at position $(i,j)$, it's connected to:
- $(i-1, j)$, $(i+1, j)$, $(i, j-1)$, $(i, j+1)$ (horizontal/vertical neighbors)
- $(i-1, j-1)$, $(i-1, j+1)$, $(i+1, j-1)$, $(i+1, j+1)$ (diagonal neighbors)

That's 8 neighbors total (in addition to the 4 orthogonal and 4 diagonal, some may not exist at boundaries).

